35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The data is stark. General rooms are always full, while specialist ones sit empty. We need space everyone can actually use.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The timetable records confirm my fears. Every room closed for works forces us to pay for off-site space for two terms.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The pattern is clear: inspection-driven work lands on time, comfort-driven work slips. Weather adds six weeks. We must price the delay, not just the bricks.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that delay cost is real. But my tender data shows mechanical plant jumped twenty percent. The paper numbers are already dead.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the market is brutal, but the people are worse. Technicians are stuck doing manual checks because the old gear fails. We need to fix the equipment, not just the budget.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, that manual labor is a symptom, not the cure. My data shows general spaces are the only ones truly valued. We must prioritize broad access over niche fixes.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree general demand is high, but the off-site costs are the real killer. We must minimize closure time to stop bleeding money.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, minimizing closure is impossible if the weather eats six weeks. We need a plan that tolerates delay, or we’re just gambling with the calendar again.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, the old gear failing is exactly why we need a reserve. We bought kit, wrote it down, but never saved to replace it. That’s a trap.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the reserve is a nice idea, but it doesn't fix the daily grind. We need to stop piling manual work on exhausted staff.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, minimizing closure is key, but we must also ensure the new space is actually booked. My data shows general access drives value, not just availability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree. But if we can’t afford the off-site replacement, we can’t close the rooms. We need a plan that avoids total shutdown.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, broad access is fine, but if the calendar slips a year, the space is useless. We need a plan that survives the weather, not just the budget.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, weather is a risk, but ignoring the twenty percent plant cost hike is a disaster. We can't build on paper numbers that don't exist.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, a plan that survives weather is useless if the staff can’t survive the workload. We need relief, not just a schedule.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Benjamin, a year of delay kills the value. My data proves general access drives usage. We need a plan that opens on time and stays open.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, I agree. But if we can’t afford the off-site replacement, we can’t close the rooms. We need a plan that avoids total shutdown.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, I hear you, but weather is a fixed cost. We need a plan that doesn’t rely on perfect conditions to finish on time.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, the manual checks prove the old gear is failing. We need a plan that doesn’t just cost more, but actually works for the people using it.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, exactly. The gear is failing, and the staff are drowning. We need a plan that fixes the equipment so the manual grind stops.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
